file digest in the manifest\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:242:(defn- manifest-address\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:246:    (testing \"one address on every host (JVM golden)\"\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:247:      (is (= manifest-golden address) (pr-str (dissoc result :links :walk))))\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:258:(deftest ^:slow manifest-address-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:259:  (slow/guard \"manifest-address-test\" manifest-address))\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:310:(def ^:private program-root-golden\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:345:              golden)\"\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:346:      (is (= program-root-golden root) (str root)))\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:347:    (testing \"a prelude revision moves the manifest address only\"\n256:  (:image (dl/adapt (ast-datoms ast))))\n261:  (:image (rc/adapt (ast-datoms ast))))\n2025:      (is (= local (lifted-value (dl/lift (:value fh))))\n2027:      (is (= local (lifted-value (rc/lift (:value fr))))\n2073:                 (lifted-value (dl/lift (:value res)))\n2075:                 :else (lifted-value (rc/lift (:value res))))))\n52:(def contract-version\n195:  [[:yin.debruijn.register/dimension :dim/contract-version contract-version]\n\n## Class 1 — Frozen non-Jing hash contracts\n\nThese call sites use `jing/sha256` (or an equivalent explicit SHA-256\nprimitive) as an independent format contract. They are not selecting an\nalgorithm from DaoJing's registry and must not be repointed at\n`default-hash-algorithm`, `content-hash`, or `segment-key`. Each has its own\nbyte rules, descriptor declarations, contract version, and golden values;\nchanging any of them is a VM- or DHT-format-version decision, not a\nDaoJing registry change.\n\n| Site | Kind | Location | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `yin.vm.debruijn-code/descriptor-hash` | `def`, computed once at namespace load | `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:524` (`jing/sha256` call at line 530) | Frozen SHA-256. Descriptor content hash under the dimension's own encoder. |\n| `yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-hash` | `defn` | `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc:531-546` | Frozen SHA-256. Computes H (S2 item 6): `sha256(descriptor-hash-hex ++ encode-image(v))`. |\n| `yin.vm.debruijn/dimension-hash` | **`def`, computed once at namespace load** — not a function | `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:944-952` | Frozen SHA-256. The published hash domain separator (§4); `(jing/sha256 (encode-value descriptor))` evaluates exactly once when the namespace loads, so every node-hash call in the process shares one already-computed value. |\n| `yin.vm.debruijn/node-hash` | `defn-` (private) | `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1002-1008` | Frozen SHA-256. `sha256(dimension-hash-hex ++ encode(slots))`, per §5. |\n| `yin.vm/primitive-profile`'s `:yin.k.pp/blake3-...` label | `defn` | `src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:351` | **No longer SHA-256.** Explicit VM contract on BLAKE3 (`(jing/content-hash description {:algorithm :blake3})`, label `blake3-`), moved with the capability seal (`engine.cljc`) and the owner tag (`values.cljc`) by the owner's decision of 2026-10-12. Computed explicitly, not by riding the default. |\n| Future register VM format contract: `register-descriptor-hash`, `register-hash` | not yet implemented | `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc` does not exist in this checkout | **Absent register implementation, recorded here as future integration.** The register design specifies format R as explicit SHA-256, mirroring the H formula (`register-descriptor-hash` parallels `descriptor-hash`; `register-hash` parallels `image-hash`). When implemented, both follow this Class-1 disposition from day one: explicit SHA-256 until the phase-8 cutover, then BLAKE3 (owner 2026-10-12), never coupled to `default-hash-algorithm`. No register golden values exist yet to preserve. |\n\nClass-1 sites never call `dao.jing/segment-key`, `dao.jing/segment-matches?`,\nor `dao.jing/materialize!`. They call `jing/sha256` (a string-in/hex-out\nprimitive independent of the address registry) or, after the H1\n`primitive-profile` fix, `jing/content-hash` with an explicit\n`{:algorithm :sha256}` — never the one-argument default form.\n\n---\n\n82:(defn- named-datoms\n87:(defn- adapted\n89:  (dl/adapt (named-datoms ast)))\n94:  (:image (adapted ast)))\n125:                              (named-datoms ast)))))\n224:      (let [adapts (map adapted programs)\n236:                   (keep :params (vals (:side-table (adapted ast)))))]\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \"0.1.30\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\n        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\n        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \"1.3\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\n ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"\n         \"build/antlr/python3/classes\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}}\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\n           :dev {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}\n                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\n                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\n                              ;; generator only; production uses\n                              ;; dao.data.btree\n                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                              {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                 :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]}\n           ;; The one ClojureDart pin. Compose it with the build aliases:\n           ;; clj -M:clojuredart:cljd ..., clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build ...\n           :clojuredart {:extra-deps {sonwh98/clojuredart\n                                      {:git/url \"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\"\n                                       :sha \"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\"}\n                                      }}\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}}\n                    :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]\n                    :main-opts [\"-m\" \"world.server\"]}\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"]}\n           :cljs-yin-repl\n           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n      ;; record value must carry no constructor metadata, on any host.\n      :list (with-meta (apply list (map canonical-value v)) nil)\n      v)))\n\n\n(defn- node-hash\n  \"§5: hash(node) = SHA-256(dimension-hash || encode(tag-specific-slots-\n   in-descriptor-order)). The preimage is the dimension hash's hex\n   followed by the framed slots under the settled byte rules; the shape —\n   descriptor order, tags, byte-count length delimiters, ordered child\n   hashes — is what D2 fixed and D3 settled. Markers are never among the\n   encodings: only present, non-marker slots reach here.\"\n  [encodings]\n  (jing/sha256 (apply str dimension-hash encodings)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; D2: hash-consing and the projected records (§4)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- slot-encodings\n",