{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md');s=p.read_text().replace('(jing/sha256 (dc/encode-scalar <printed descriptor>))','(jing/blake3 (dc/encode-scalar <printed descriptor>))').replace('differs from the previous one only by the removed \"'`:dim/lift-to` row and, if the arity row counts it, by nothing else'\"','differs by exactly the removed \"'`:dim/lift-to` row and the `:hash` value'\"');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/design/dao.jing.hash-registry.md');s=p.read_text();a=s.index('The four de Bruijn hashes');b=s.index('### Primitive-profile identifier',a);s=s[:a]+'''The six surviving de Bruijn hash sites use explicit BLAKE3 after the\nphase-8ab regeneration (2026-10-14): stack and register descriptor hashes,\nH and R checksums, and the projection dimension and node hashes. Their\nencoders remain independent of DaoJing's addressing encoder and minting\ndefault. A is the sole code identity; H and R are derived checksums.\n\nThe DHT node ID remains SHA-256 because it defines the DHT routing\nidentity space. Changing it is a separate DHT protocol decision.\n\n'''+s[b:];a=s.index('H and R remain explicitly SHA-256.');b=s.index('Jing addresses for stored',a);s=s[:a]+'''Phase 8ab regenerates H and R with explicit \"'`jing/blake3`, and both\ndescriptor encoding rows declare `:hash :blake3`. The obsolete\n`:dim/lift-to` rows are removed. `lowering-contract-version` 2 and\n`contract-version` 4 remain unchanged under owner ruling 2; this is a\nregeneration, with no compatibility shim. Projection dimension and node\nhashes also use explicit BLAKE3. Every pin is recomputable from printed\nintermediates (derivations §8.1).\n\nA is the sole code identity. H and R are checksums of derived backend\nimages, with their own canonical encoders and descriptor hashes; they\nnever follow `default-hash-algorithm`.\n\n'\"'''+s[b:];s=s.replace('H or R, identifying its executable-format bytes','H or R, checking its derived backend-format bytes').replace('That code serves both the first-class SHA-256 registry entry and the explicit VM/DHT contracts.','That code serves the first-class SHA-256 registry entry and the explicit DHT contract.').replace('yin.vm documentation states that H/R remain SHA-256 because of VM contract freeze, not compatibility policy or DaoJing\\\\'s default;','yin.vm documentation records the phase-8ab explicit BLAKE3 regeneration of H/R, independent of DaoJing\\\\'s default;').replace('- Unchanged stack H and de Bruijn format-hash goldens.\\\\n- Unchanged R goldens when register code lands.','- Stack H, R and de Bruijn format-hash goldens regenerated at phase 8ab.');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/design/dao.jing.call-site-classification.md');s=p.read_text();a=s.index('These call sites use');b=s.index('\\\\n---',a);s=s[:a]+'''These sites use explicit primitives as independent format contracts.\nThey never follow \"'`default-hash-algorithm`. Phase 8ab regenerates all six\nsurviving de Bruijn hashes with BLAKE3, retaining contract versions 2 and\n4 (owner ruling 2). A is the sole code identity; H and R are derived\nchecksums. DHT routing identity remains explicit SHA-256.\n\n| Site | Kind | Location | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `yin.vm.debruijn-code/descriptor-hash` | `def` | `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc` | Explicit `jing/blake3` over `encode-scalar descriptor`. |\n| `yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-hash` | `defn` | same | H = `blake3(descriptor-hash-hex ++ encode-image(v))`. |\n| `yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/descriptor-hash` | `def` | `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc` | Explicit `jing/blake3` over `debruijn-code/encode-scalar descriptor`. |\n| `yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-hash` | `defn` | same | R = `blake3(descriptor-hash-hex ++ encode-register-image(image))`. |\n| `yin.vm.debruijn/dimension-hash` | `def`, computed once at namespace load | `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc` | Explicit `jing/blake3` over `encode-value descriptor`. |\n| `yin.vm.debruijn/node-hash` | private `defn-` | same | `blake3(dimension-hash-hex ++ encode(slots))`, per §5. |\n| `yin.vm/primitive-profile` | `defn` | `src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc` | Explicit `jing/content-hash` with `{:algorithm :blake3}`; label `blake3-`. |\n\nThe six de Bruijn sites call the string-in/hex-out `jing/blake3` primitive;\nthey do not mint Jing addresses. Primitive profiles explicitly select\nBLAKE3 through `content-hash`. DHT node IDs use `jing/sha256`. None uses\nthe one-argument minting default.\n'\"'''+s[b:];s=s.replace('**4** frozen Class-1 SHA-256 contracts implemented today (the DHT node id is derived by the composition, not in \"'`dht.cljc`), plus **1**'\"','**6** explicit Class-1 BLAKE3 de Bruijn sites implemented today, plus **1**');p.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
