{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '235,280p' test/yin/vm/ucf/handoff_v2_census_test.cljc; sed -n '160,177p' target/8ab/vm-quick.log; sed -n '334,352p' target/8ab/vm-quick.log; rg --files test/resources/yin/vm/ucf; sed -n '1,65p' test/yin/vm/ucf/handoff_v2_census_test.cljc; rg -n 'fixtures|handoff-v2|mint' test/yin/vm/ucf/handoff_v2_census_test.cljc test/yin/vm/ucf/v2_support.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   lowercase hex in lines of 64 digits.  Regenerate with `golden-text`.\"\n  \"test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/handoff-v2.txt\")\n\n\n(defn- golden-text\n  [export]\n  (let [h (fx/bytes->hex (:bytes export))]\n    (str \"handoff-v2-stack-float-literal\\n\"\n         (subs (str (:address export)) 1) \"\\n\"\n         (apply str (map #(str (subs h % (min (count h) (+ % 64))) \"\\n\")\n                         (range 0 (count h) 64))))))\n\n\n(deftest a-version-2-body-is-the-same-bytes-on-every-host\n  (let [[export src t peer] (lift-float-literal :stack)\n        [n address & hex] (str/split-lines (fx/read-path golden-path))\n        pinned (fx/hex->bytes (apply str hex))\n        [r _] (s/read! :stack t pinned\n                       {:address (keyword \"segment\"\n                                          (subs address (count \"segment/\")))})]\n    (is (= :ok (:status export)) (pr-str export))\n    (is (= \"handoff-v2-stack-float-literal\" n))\n    (is (= address (subs (str (:address export)) 1))\n        (str \"this host's lift differs from the pinned address; were the\n              change intended, regenerate:\\n\" (golden-text export)))\n    (is (= (apply str hex) (fx/bytes->hex (:bytes export)))\n        \"this host lifts the pinned bytes exactly\")\n    (is (= 2 (:yin.k/version (jing.cbor/decode pinned))))\n    (is (contains? (code-floats (jing.cbor/decode pinned))\n                   (enc (jing.cbor/float64 -0.0))))\n    (is (= :ok (:status r)) \"the pinned bytes lower on this host\")\n    (when (:vm r)\n      (stream/append! src \"B\")\n      (carriers-ok (vm/value (s/drive (:vm r) peer))))))\n\nTesting yin.vm.ucf.handoff-test\n\nTesting yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v1-test\n\nTesting yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v2-authority-test\n\nTesting yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v2-census-test\n\nFAIL in (a-version-2-body-is-the-same-bytes-on-every-host) (handoff_v2_census_test.cljc:257)\nthis host's lift differs from the pinned address; were the\n              change intended, regenerate:\nhandoff-v2-stack-float-literal\nsegment/blake3-52c7efaa3967b16b4b77f913b77b91d054f739c7a8bf1239f090aca3a53ecd70\nafd81b827064616f2e6a696e672f6b6579776f7264826579696e2e6b64636f64\n65a1784036383862326234353061616333373066336135353032313539633564\n3839363434336336333039623536646366353065626637633232616330303034\n663135359683d81b827064616f2e6a696e672f6b6579776f726482f667636c6f\n6b6579776f7264826579696e2e6b6a69642d636f756e74657202d81b82706461\n6f2e6a696e672f6b6579776f7264826579696e2e6b6d6d6f64756c652d73746f\n726573a0\n\nexpected: (= address (subs (str (:address export)) 1))\n  actual: (not (= \"segment/blake3-afe9e3ac1c3c29e377dbba5a6ec27d5da8382e97515e2dac21a5cd7797369f10\" \"segment/blake3-52c7efaa3967b16b4b77f913b77b91d054f739c7a8bf1239f090aca3a53ecd70\"))\n\nFAIL in (a-version-2-body-is-the-same-bytes-on-every-host) (handoff_v2_census_test.cljc:260)\nthis host lifts the pinned bytes exactly\nexpected: (= (apply str hex) (fx/bytes->hex (:bytes export)))\n  actual: (not (= \"\" \"\"))\n\nFAIL in (a-version-2-body-is-the-same-bytes-on-every-host) (handoff_v2_census_test.cljc:265)\nthe pinned bytes lower on this host\nexpected: (= :ok (:status r))\n  actual: (not (= :ok nil))\n\nTesting yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v2-custody-test\n\ntest/resources/yin/vm/ucf/scalars-v1.txt\ntest/resources/yin/vm/ucf/ledger-v2.txt\ntest/resources/yin/vm/ucf/checkpoint-v1.txt\ntest/resources/yin/vm/ucf/scalars-v1.mint.clj\ntest/resources/yin/vm/ucf/rows-checkpoint-v3.txt\ntest/resources/yin/vm/ucf/handoff-v2.txt\n(ns yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v2-census-test\n  \"UCF version 2, section 11 rows 3, 4 and 10: the census.  Aliased and\n   independent cells keep their identities across ordered waits; a halted\n   result carries a linked module's closure with its store and image and\n   no initialization reruns on lower; numeric carrier classes (float64\n   integral content, negative zero) survive in code and value positions\n   without recomputing a code hash after coercion.\"\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as jing.cbor]\n            [dao.jing.cbor-fixtures :as fx]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.handoff :as handoff]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n\n\n(defn- ordered-waits\n  \"`parked`, a reader, with four ordered waits: the original, a second\n   waiter on the same cell, and two independent cells at one position.\"\n  [parked]\n  (let [base (first (:wait-set parked))\n        cid (get-in base [:cursor-ref :id])\n        sid (:stream-id base)\n        kept (get-in parked [:resources cid :cursor])\n        indep (fn [id] (assoc base :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id id}))]\n    (-> parked\n        (update :resources assoc\n                :yin/i1 {:stream-id sid :cursor kept}\n                :yin/i2 {:stream-id sid :cursor kept})\n        (assoc :wait-set [base base (indep :yin/i1) (indep :yin/i2)]))))\n\n\n(deftest aliased-and-independent-cells-survive-ordered-waits\n  (doseq [engine s/engines]\n    (testing (name engine)\n      (let [[parked _] (s/parked-reader engine)\n            four (ordered-waits parked)\n            t (s/toy)\n            peer (s/served-peer t)\n            export (s/lift four t peer)\n            body (:body export)\n            cells-of (fn [m]\n                       (mapv #(get-in % [:cursor-ref :id]) (:wait-set m)))\n            [r _] (s/read! engine t (:bytes export)\n                           {:address (:address export)})\n            ids (cells-of (:vm r))\n            pendings (mapv :yin.k/pending (:yin.k/frames body))]\n        (is (= :ok (:status export)) (pr-str export))\n        (is (= 4 (count (:yin.k/frames body))) \"the wait order is kept\")\n        (is (= 3 (count (:yin.k/cells body)))\n            \"one cell for the aliases, one each for the independents\")\n        (is (= (:yin.k/cell (first pendings)) (:yin.k/cell (second pendings))))\n        (is (not= (:yin.k/cell (second pendings))\n                  (:yin.k/cell (nth pendings 2))))\n        (is (not= (:yin.k/cell (nth pendings 2))\n                  (:yin.k/cell (nth pendings 3))))\n        (is (= :ok (:status r)) (pr-str r))\n        (is (= (first ids) (second ids)))\n        (is (= 3 (count (set ids))) \"three fresh cursor entries\")))))\n\n\n(defn- link-through\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/v2_support.cljc:363:                 :call-out-cursor (vm/mint-oldest call-out :test)\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/handoff_v2_census_test.cljc:1:(ns yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v2-census-test\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/handoff_v2_census_test.cljc:11:            [dao.jing.cbor-fixtures :as fx]\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/handoff_v2_census_test.cljc:236:  \"test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/handoff-v2.txt\")\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/handoff_v2_census_test.cljc:242:    (str \"handoff-v2-stack-float-literal\\n\"\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/handoff_v2_census_test.cljc:256:    (is (= \"handoff-v2-stack-float-literal\" n))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
