{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_98","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nlines=Path('target/8ab/regen-1.edn').read_text().splitlines(); entries=[x for x in lines if x.startswith('[\\\"')]; new=[re.findall(r'[0-9a-f]{64}',x)[-1] for x in entries];print('Entries',len(entries),'distinct new values',len(set(new)))\nPY\nsed -n '28,48p' collab/1792620000000-engineer-8ab.report.md; sed -n '345,364p' docs/design/dao.jing.hash-registry.md; tail -4 target/8ab/lint.log\"","aggregated_output":"Entries 51 distinct new values 50\nRun from the repository root:\n\n```sh\nclojure -M collab/1792620000000-8ab-regen.clj\n```\n\n[The script](./1792620000000-8ab-regen.clj) is 42 lines. Its\n[printed intermediates](./1792620000000-8ab-intermediates.edn) contain all\nimages, descriptors, ASTs and manifest maps. It uses only public functions;\nno old lowerer, private var, test namespace or network is needed. Projection\nroots are regenerated from their whole AST, so child hashes also regenerate.\nThe four literal-double fingerprints take the same public projection path\nas their tests. The H/R image bytes remain pinned in the tests.\n\nThe script also reconstructs and verifies the handoff fixture wire bytes.\nTwo final runs produced byte-identical stdout (`cmp`, exit 0), covering 51\ndistinct constants. The H descriptor's old checksum was previously unpinned;\nits new checksum is pinned. Repeated occurrences of the worked-example H\n(derive, linker and parity) are one constant in this table. The register\nlinker golden has its own new `derive` image; the old compiler's checksum of\nits different allocation remains a separate entry.\n### Explicit hash contracts\n\nThe six de Bruijn consumers and the DHT routing hash are independent of\nDaoJing's minting default. They have their own encoders and contracts.\n\nThe six surviving de Bruijn hash sites use explicit BLAKE3 after the\nphase-8ab regeneration (2026-10-14): stack and register descriptor hashes,\nH and R checksums, and the projection dimension and node hashes. Their\nencoders remain independent of DaoJing's addressing encoder and minting\ndefault. A is the sole code identity; H and R are derived checksums.\n\nThe DHT node ID remains SHA-256 because it defines the DHT routing\nidentity space. Changing it is a separate DHT protocol decision.\n\n### Primitive-profile identifier\n\n`yin.vm/primitive-profile` constructs:\n\n```clojure\n:yin.k.pp/blake3-<digest of (content-hash description {:algorithm :blake3})>\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\nlinting took 8284ms, errors: 0, warnings: 0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
